## Known limitations

- Performance measured on the supplied Bayan evaluation data may not represent all real-world citizen feedback.
- Some evaluation slices contain fewer examples than others, so their estimates are less precise.
- Validation errors show a repeated confusion between the `parks` and `roads` topic classes.
- The observed classification errors are concentrated in Arabic MSA examples.
- Behavioural tests cover selected expected behaviours and do not represent every possible production input.
- Strong performance on the supplied evaluation sets does not guarantee the same performance on unseen data.

